Assuming you're using Windows XP (probably works for other Windows too):

  Alt-Enter will maximize a DOS window.
Then, type

  mode con:lines=25   (older DOSes use the more sensible "mode co80")

at the prompt.  If nothing happens, good.  If the text on your screen
becomes taller, then also good -- but it means you should change the
defaults on your DOS window.
  You can do that by opening a new DOS window, *not* maximizing it,
right-click the upper-left-hand corner, select "Defaults," and then
change "Window Size: Height" to "25".

